# Rendered output. Every PNG here is reproducible from decks/ with one command,
# and committing them once put 900MB of binaries in a repo whose source is under
# 2MB. Render, do not store.
out/

# Post-ready JPEG/MP4 exports, wherever they land.
_post/

# Theme previews. `previews.js` builds each pack a contact sheet of its own
# output, which is exactly what you want locally and exactly what you do not
# want committed: they are 40MB of PNG against 2MB of source, and each one is
# rendered from whatever deck declares that theme — usually a decks/.local/ one
# carrying your handle and your blog copy. Rebuild, do not store:
#   node scripts/previews.js --all
themes/*/preview.png

node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Personal decks. `decks/` ships a few neutral examples; anything with your own
# handle, blog content or client work goes here and stays out of the repo.
# Still renders normally: node scripts/render.js decks/.local/<slug>.json out/<slug>
decks/.local/

# Original 3dicons SVG downloads. `ingest-3dicons.js` rasterises these into
# assets/objects-3d/ at 512px; nothing reads the SVGs at render time. They are
# 279MB against 50MB for the PNGs actually used. Keep them locally if you want
# to re-export at another size — do not ship them.
assets/3dicons - */
